    {
      "tag": "SPAN",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "faq-question-text",
      "text": "Is Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu safe for beginners?",
      "font": 15.68,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 40.78125,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 1964.796875,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "direct-answer fw-semibold text-dark mb-2",
      "text": "Yes. Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu at Sensei Sandy BJJ is safe for beginners. Training begins with a studio tour, a safety walkthrough, and clear rules. Every drill is coach-led with carefully matched partners, controlled movement, and mutual tapping. You set your own pace from day one.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 235.46875,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 2021.578125,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "text-muted mb-3",
      "text": "Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu is a grappling martial art based on leverage, balance, and body position rather than striking. At our Tannersville studio, class size is capped at 12 students so Coach Sandy can guide every partner interaction. Students learn how to fall safely, how to tap to signal a reset, and how to practice with care. Beginners start in our Beginner Lane, practicing cooperative movement at a calm, comfortable pace.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 353.203125,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 2269.046875,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "btn-link-pill small",
      "text": "See Class Safety Guide",
      "font": 12.88,
      "width": 161.078125,
      "height": 44,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 2638.25,
      "position": "static",
      "href": "/jiu-jitsu-safety-tannersville-ny"
    },
    {
      "tag": "SPAN",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "faq-question-text",
      "text": "At what age can children start BJJ?",
      "font": 15.68,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 40.78125,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 2734.25,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "direct-answer fw-semibold text-dark mb-2",
      "text": "Children can start Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu at age 5 at Sensei Sandy BJJ. Our Youth classes welcome kids ages 5 to 9, and our Teen classes serve youth ages 10 to 17. Younger children learn through active movement games that build balance, focus, and body control.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 235.46875,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 2791.03125,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "text-muted mb-3",
      "text": "For kids ages 5 to 9, classes focus on body awareness, coordination, following coach directions, and working respectfully with a partner. We teach children how to move safely, protect their heads, and solve physical problems using leverage. Parents are always welcome to stay and watch every youth class from matside.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 282.5625,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 3038.5,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "btn-link-pill small",
      "text": "Explore Kids Classes",
      "font": 12.88,
      "width": 144.9375,
      "height": 44,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 3337.0625,
      "position": "static",
      "href": "/bjj-classes/kids-tannersville-ny"
    },
    {
      "tag": "SPAN",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "faq-question-text",
      "text": "Do I need to be physically fit before starting?",
      "font": 15.68,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 40.78125,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 3433.0625,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "direct-answer fw-semibold text-dark mb-2",
      "text": "You can start Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu at any fitness level. Training is how you build stamina, strength, and mobility. Classes begin with calm, coach-guided pacing, and Coach Sandy adjusts each activity to fit your current comfort.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 211.921875,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 3489.84375,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "text-muted mb-3",
      "text": "Adults of all backgrounds and body types train at Sensei Sandy BJJ. We prioritize leverage and technique over brute force. You can pause, rest, or adjust intensity during any drill. Simply wear comfortable athletic clothes and start at your own speed.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 211.921875,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 3713.765625,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "btn-link-pill small",
      "text": "Explore Adult Beginner Lane",
      "font": 12.88,
      "width": 197.171875,
      "height": 44,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 3941.6875,
      "position": "static",
      "href": "/bjj-classes/adults-tannersville-ny"
    },
    {
      "tag": "SPAN",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "faq-question-text",
      "text": "What should I expect during my first BJJ class?",
      "font": 15.68,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 40.78125,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4037.6875,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "direct-answer fw-semibold text-dark mb-2",
      "text": "Your first visit begins with a 15-minute room tour and conversation with Coach Sandy. You see the clean mats, learn studio safety rules, and discuss your personal goals. For your first coached class, you are paired with a calm, experienced partner for gentle, step-by-step movement drills.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 259.015625,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4094.46875,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "text-muted mb-3",
      "text": "You will experience pure encouragement and cooperative learning from day one. You wear comfortable athletic clothes. Coach Sandy introduces fundamental positions, safe movement, and how tapping allows partners to reset comfortably. You will always know what comes next, and you can ask questions at any point. Your first class is a free coached learning experience.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 329.65625,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4365.484375,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "btn-link-pill small",
      "text": "See How Class Works",
      "font": 12.88,
      "width": 150.15625,
      "height": 44,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4711.140625,
      "position": "static",
      "href": "/how-class-works"
    },
    {
      "tag": "SPAN",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "faq-question-text",
      "text": "How do I choose the right martial arts school?",
      "font": 15.68,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 40.78125,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4128.46875,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "direct-answer fw-semibold text-dark mb-2",
      "text": "Start with a visit. Meet the coach and watch a class. Look for small class sizes, so the coach can see every student and give clear steps. Look for a calm room and partners who train with care. Ask how new students begin. A good school gives you a clear first step and room to learn at your pace.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 259.015625,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4185.25,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "text-muted mb-3",
      "text": "At Sensei Sandy BJJ, classes are capped at 12 students, and Sandy coaches every class himself. Your first visit is free. You can watch first, then join in when you feel ready. Reserve Free Intro. Start calm. Train smart.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 188.375,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4456.265625,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "btn-link-pill small",
      "text": "Reserve Free Intro",
      "font": 12.88,
      "width": 133.875,
      "height": 44,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4660.640625,
      "position": "static",
      "href": "/free-bjj-intro-tannersville-ny#booking-flow"
    },
    {
      "tag": "SPAN",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "faq-question-text",
      "text": "How often should beginners train?",
      "font": 15.68,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 40.78125,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4219.25,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "direct-answer fw-semibold text-dark mb-2",
      "text": "Beginners progress best by training 2 to 3 times per week. This rhythm gives your body adequate time to recover while reinforcing new movement patterns, muscle memory, and positional awareness each week.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 188.375,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4276.03125,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "text-muted mb-3",
      "text": "Consistency matters more than intensity. Attending two or three small-group classes each week allows techniques to feel natural and comfortable. Our schedule offers weekday youth classes at 5:00 PM, adult classes at 6:00 PM, and Saturday morning sessions, with open-seat rescheduling by text if family or work plans change.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 282.5625,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4476.40625,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "btn-link-pill small",
      "text": "View Weekly Schedule",
      "font": 12.88,
      "width": 156.984375,
      "height": 44,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4774.96875,
      "position": "static",
      "href": "/schedule"
    },
    {
      "tag": "SPAN",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "faq-question-text",
      "text": "Does Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu help build children's confidence?",
      "font": 15.68,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 61.171875,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4310.03125,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "direct-answer fw-semibold text-dark mb-2",
      "text": "Yes. Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu builds genuine confidence through earned accomplishment. By learning how to escape holds, protect their balance, and solve physical challenges against gentle resistance, children discover they can handle difficult situations with calm focus.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 235.46875,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4387.203125,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "text-muted mb-3",
      "text": "Unlike activities based on rote memorization, Jiu-Jitsu gives children tangible feedback in real time. They see their progress as they learn to defend themselves, respect training partners, and speak up when they need help. Parents frequently report improvements in focus at school, better emotional control at home, and quiet self-assurance.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 306.109375,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4634.671875,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "btn-link-pill small",
      "text": "Read Parent Reviews",
      "font": 12.88,
      "width": 148.484375,
      "height": 44,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4956.78125,
      "position": "static",
      "href": "/parent-resources"
    },
    {
      "tag": "SPAN",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "faq-question-text",
      "text": "Where can I take Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu classes near Hunter or Tannersville?",
      "font": 15.68,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 61.171875,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4421.203125,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "direct-answer fw-semibold text-dark mb-2",
      "text": "You can take Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu classes at Sensei Sandy BJJ, located at 6045 Main Street (2nd Floor Studio) in Tannersville, NY. The studio is just 4 miles from Hunter and easily accessible from Windham, Haines Falls, and Mountaintop communities across the Catskills.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 235.46875,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4498.375,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "text-muted mb-3",
      "text": "We are located right on Main Street in Tannersville, inside Studios on Main, with ample street parking nearby. We offer dedicated classes for Kids (ages 5–9), Teens (ages 10–17), and Adults (18+), as well as private morning coaching. Families and visitors traveling from Hunter, Windham, Phoenicia, and Catskill can book a Free First Visit to meet Coach Sandy and tour the academy.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 329.65625,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4745.84375,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "btn-link-pill small",
      "text": "Get Directions & Parking",
      "font": 12.88,
      "width": 172.9375,
      "height": 44,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 5091.5,
      "position": "static",
      "href": "/bjj-tannersville-ny-directions"
    },
    {
      "tag": "SPAN",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "faq-question-text",
      "text": "What should I wear to my first class?",
      "font": 15.68,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 40.78125,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4532.375,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "direct-answer fw-semibold text-dark mb-2",
      "text": "Wear clean, comfortable athletic clothing, such as a t-shirt or rash guard and athletic shorts or sweatpants. Choose clothing free of zippers, snaps, buttons, or metal hardware to protect your partners and the mats.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 188.375,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4589.15625,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "text-muted mb-3",
      "text": "You train in bare feet on clean mats. We recommend bringing a water bottle and slip-on shoes or flip-flops to wear off the mat. We provide loaner gis and uniforms for subsequent classes.",
      "font": 14.72,
      "width": 226,
      "height": 164.828125,
      "x": 85,
      "y": 4789.53125,
      "position": "static",
      "href": null
    },
    {
